RINGKASAN (Bahasa Indonesia, tidak mengikat; teks yang mengikat ada di bawah)

- Kode (core/, tools/, plugin/, kode demo): MIT. Bebas dipakai, diubah, dan
  dibagikan, termasuk untuk komersial, asal notice hak cipta di file ini ikut.
- Panduan dan prompt gaya (semua file .md): CC BY-NC 4.0. Bebas dipakai,
  diubah, dan dibagikan secara non-komersial dengan mencantumkan kredit.
  Untuk membuat film sendiri, termasuk film komersial dan film klien, ada izin
  tambahan (lihat bagian 3).
- Still dan subtitle film demo: CC BY 4.0.
- Terjemahan, branding Code Cinema, dan alur kerja berbahasa Indonesia:
  (c) 2026 Mega Bagus Herlambang, dengan lisensi yang sama (MIT untuk kode,
  CC BY-NC 4.0 untuk teks).
- Film yang Anda buat dengan alat ini sepenuhnya milik Anda, termasuk untuk
  komersial, tanpa kewajiban kredit.
- Materi pihak ketiga (font, musik, sampel, footage, foto, data, peta) tetap
  memakai lisensinya masing-masing, seperti tercantum di CREDITS setiap demo.


1. ORIGIN AND COPYRIGHT

Code Cinema is a modified, Indonesian-language edition of the Lemo-Opuscar
library (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), created by Lemomo.

  Original work: Copyright (c) 2026 SecondFirst Pty Ltd, trading as LemoLab.
  Changes and additions: Copyright (c) 2026 Mega Bagus Herlambang (megabagus,
  https://github.com/pendekarAI).

Changes made by Mega Bagus Herlambang: the project, skill, paths, variables
and on-screen sign-offs were renamed; the main guides (README.md, AGENTS.md,
DIRECTOR.md, TECHNIQUE.md, MY-STYLES.md, styles/README.md and the skill) were
translated into Indonesian and adapted; maintainer-only tools, the gallery
site, posters, two stills and one demo (Mascot Screencast) were removed; the
large asset packs are re-hosted on this repository's "assets" release.

The full licence texts are in LICENSES/. The first rule below that matches a
file decides its licence.


2. WHICH LICENCE APPLIES

2.1 Third-party material keeps its own licence or terms: fonts and their
    licence texts, music, sound recordings and sample libraries, models and
    textures, data, maps, footage, photographs, and the code libraries bundled
    with some demos. Each demo's CREDITS (styles/<slug>/demo/CREDITS) names the
    material, its source and its licence. See also
    LICENSES/LicenseRef-PublicDomain.txt, LICENSES/LicenseRef-IBTrACS.txt and
    LICENSES/LicenseRef-ThirdPartyMarks.txt.

2.2 Docs: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
    (CC BY-NC 4.0, LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt,
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).
    - Every Markdown file (*.md): the guides, each style's STYLE.md and
      DEMO.md, the READMEs and the skill's SKILL.md, in their original and in
      their translated or adapted form.
    - The image-generation prompts: everything under styles/*/demo/prompts/,
      styles/manga-panels/demo/tools/style_suffix.txt and
      styles/comic-history/demo/tools/sheets.json.

2.3 Demo stills and subtitles: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
    (CC BY 4.0, LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt,
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
    - styles/*/demo/stills/ and styles/*/*.srt. Third-party material shown in
      them keeps its own licence (2.1).

2.4 Code: MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt). Everything else: the code in core/,
    tools/ and plugin/ and each demo's code, with the data, configuration,
    CREDITS and small assets they use. The MIT notice for this material is:

      Copyright (c) 2026 SecondFirst Pty Ltd, trading as LemoLab
      Copyright (c) 2026 Mega Bagus Herlambang

    Where the MIT text speaks of "this software and associated documentation
    files", it means the material under this rule only, not the docs of 2.2.

Two styles were contributed to the original library from outside and are
included with their authors' permission: Memphis Diorama by EianLu
(styles/memphis-diorama/) and Crayon World 3D by 2nd1st (styles/crayon-world/).

Third-party product names, interfaces, logos and trademarks that appear in the
demos belong to their owners and are not licensed here.


3. FILMS YOU MAKE, AND ADDITIONAL PERMISSION FOR THE DOCS

Films you make with the library are yours, commercial films included, and need
no credit; third-party material you use in them keeps its own terms.

The original licensor grants, in addition to CC BY-NC 4.0, a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable permission to you and the people
working with you on a film (staff, contractors, the client) to read, follow,
copy and adapt the docs to make your own films (commercial and client films
included), and to include them, or versions you adapted, in the project files
you deliver for that film. A style you change and keep as your own to make
your films (MY-STYLES.md) is covered. Mega Bagus Herlambang grants the same
permission for his translations and additions. This permission does not cover
sharing the docs or adapted versions with others beyond those people and those
project files, or selling them: CC BY-NC 4.0 governs those. Any other
commercial use of the original docs (for example selling them, or putting them
into a product or service run for commercial advantage) needs a commercial
licence from the original licensor.


4. HOW TO CREDIT

When you share this library or parts of it:

  "Code Cinema by Mega Bagus Herlambang, based on Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo
  (LemoLab)", with a link to https://github.com/pendekarAI/code-cinema, the
  name of the licence with a link to it (CC BY-NC 4.0 for the docs, CC BY 4.0
  for the stills and subtitles, MIT for the code), and say if you changed it.

For the two contributed styles, name their author too: "Memphis Diorama by
EianLu" and "Crayon World 3D by 2nd1st".

Third-party material is credited as its CREDITS says.
